│ Okay, so I need to figure out exactly what "ordered       │   keys: ['Control', 'a']                                  │
│ exactly 100 times" means in the context of the Metabase   │   intent: Select all text in editor                       │
│ Sample Database. My initial thought is to replace the     │                                                           │
│ text with my query. However, let's pause. I need to make  │                                                           │
│ sure I understand the core concept first. Does it mean a  │                                                           │
│ specific product was part of 100 *individual* orders      │                                                           │
│ (that is, `COUNT(*)`), or did the quantity of that        │                                                           │
│ product in orders add up to 100 units total (that would   │                                                           │
│ be `SUM(QUANTITY)`) or is it `COUNT(PRODUCT_ID)`?         │                                                           │
│                                                           │                                                           │
│ I need to cover my bases and check both possibilities. My │                                                           │
│ plan is to write a SQL query that will give me both       │                                                           │
│ counts. I'll join the `PRODUCTS` and `ORDERS` tables,     │                                                           │
│ grouping by product details and then calculate both the   │                                                           │
│ number of orders (`COUNT(o.id)`) and the total quantity   │                                                           │
│ ordered (`SUM(o.quantity)`). Finally, I'll filter using a │                                                           │
│ `HAVING` clause to identify products where *either* of    │                                                           │
│ those values is exactly 100. I'll order by the product's  │                                                           │
│ price, for good measure.                                  │                                                           │
│                                                           │                                                           │
│ I think I have a working query now, let's execute the     │                                                           │
│ query now to find any products with either count or sum   │                                                           │
│ equal to 100:                                             │                                                           │
│ ```sql                                                    │                                                           │
│ SELECT p.id, p.title, p.category, p.price, COUNT(o.id) as │                                                           │
│ order_count, SUM(o.quantity) as total_quantity            │                                                           │
│ FROM products p                                           │                                                           │
│ JOIN orders o ON p.id = o.product_id                      │                                                           │
│ GROUP BY p.id, p.title, p.category, p.price               │                                                           │
│ HAVING COUNT(o.id) = 100 OR SUM(o.quantity) = 100         │                                                           │
│ ORDER BY p.price ASC;                                     │                                                           │
│ ```                                                       │                                                           │
